{
  "id": "temporal-conditioning",
  "term": "temporal conditioning",
  "definition": "Temporal conditioning is a form of learning in which behavior comes under the control of time, so an organism begins to respond in anticipation of an event that occurs at regular intervals even without external cues. In the supplied example, mice learned to increase licking near the expected time of reward delivery.",
